---
// Four Laws conversion point → site waitlist (/#notify). One form, not duplicated per page.
---

<aside class="cta-block">
	<span class="label kicker">From the author</span>
	<p class="lede">
		These laws are the vocabulary I use in the field. If you're running a
		founder-led professional services firm and something structural keeps
		breaking, I write diagnoses — not implementations.
	</p>
	<a class="cta" href="/#notify">
		See what that is &rarr;
	</a>
</aside>

<style>
	/* Sage left rule (not mustard): shows on every content page; mustard stays for outliers. */
	.cta-block {
		margin: 3.5rem 0 0;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--sage);
	}
	.kicker {
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		color: var(--sage);
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.lede {
		margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
		font-size: 0.97rem;
	}
	.cta {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
	}
	.cta:hover {
		border-bottom-color: var(--plum);
	}
</style>
